---Properties for Redis Enterprise migration operation for Azure Cache for Redis.
---@class azure.redisenterprise.AzureCacheForRedisMigrationProperties
---@field sourceType azure.redisenterprise.AzureCacheForRedisMigrationPropertiesSourceType Describes the source of the migration operation.
---@field targetResourceId? string The Azure resource ID of the Azure Managed Redis destination cache to migrate.
---@field provisioningState? azure.redisenterprise.MigrationProvisioningState Current provisioning status of the migration
---@field statusDetails? string|distilled.Null Additional details about the migration operation's status in free text format.
---@field creationTime? string The timestamp when the migration operation was created.
---@field lastModifiedTime? string The timestamp when the migration operation was last updated.
---@field rollbackEligibleUntil? string The timestamp until which a successful migration remains eligible to be undone (rolled back) to the source cache. This property is only returned while the migration is in the Succeeded state, and is calculated from the time the migration succeeded plus the rollback window. After this time the source cache is released and the migration can no longer be undone.
---@field sourceResourceId string The source resource ID to migrate from. This is the resource ID of the Azure Cache for Redis.
---@field switchDns boolean Sets whether the DNS is switched automatically after the data is transferred from the source cache to the target cache. This property must be true during the preview.
---@field skipDataMigration boolean Sets whether the data is migrated from source to target or not. Set this property to true to skip data migration.
---@field forceMigrate? boolean Sets whether to ignore warnings when performing validation of the migration request. If this property is true, warning-level disparities between the source and target resources will be ignored, and the request will only fail validation if there are error-level disparities. The default value is false.

