---Properties for creating Redis Enterprise databases
---@class azure.redisenterprise.DatabaseCreateProperties
---@field clientProtocol? azure.redisenterprise.Protocol Specifies whether redis clients can connect using TLS-encrypted or plaintext redis protocols. Default is TLS-encrypted.
---@field port? number TCP port of the database endpoint. Specified at create time. Defaults to an available port.
---@field provisioningState? azure.redisenterprise.ProvisioningState Current provisioning status of the database
---@field resourceState? azure.redisenterprise.ResourceState Current resource status of the database
---@field clusteringPolicy? azure.redisenterprise.ClusteringPolicy Clustering policy - default is OSSCluster. This property can be updated only if the current value is NoCluster. If the value is OSSCluster or EnterpriseCluster, it cannot be updated without deleting the database.
---@field evictionPolicy? azure.redisenterprise.EvictionPolicy Redis eviction policy - default is VolatileLRU
---@field persistence? azure.redisenterprise.Persistence Persistence settings
---@field modules? azure.redisenterprise.DatabaseCreatePropertiesModulesList Optional set of redis modules to enable in this database - modules can only be added at creation time.
---@field geoReplication? azure.redisenterprise.DatabasePropertiesGeoReplication Optional set of properties to configure geo replication for this database.
---@field redisVersion? string Version of Redis the database is running on, e.g. '6.0'
---@field deferUpgrade? azure.redisenterprise.DeferUpgradeSetting Option to defer upgrade when newest version is released - default is NotDeferred. Learn more: https://aka.ms/redisversionupgrade
---@field accessKeysAuthentication? azure.redisenterprise.AccessKeysAuthentication This property can be Enabled/Disabled to allow or deny access with the current access keys. Can be updated even after database is created.
---@field notifyKeyspaceEvents? string Specifies which keyspace events should trigger notifications. Default is an empty string, meaning this feature is disabled. When enabled, at least 'K' (keyspace events) or 'E' (keyevent events) must be present. For example, 'AKE' enables all standard events. See https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/use/keyspace-notifications/ for the complete list of event types.

